From 728b1cb9b0bb83efe9c4d6a8f8863078570d1751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:14:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/30] allwinner: h713: wait 20 ms for crust to start, with
 room for its init to grow

The 12 ms BL31 waits for MAGIC and RUNNING were five times the model time
of an older v4 image and had no room left: with the crust images of
07.10.2026 an instruction-level AR100 model (8 cycles per instruction at
24 MHz, the slowest clock the SPL may leave it on) counts 7154
instructions to RUNNING for the SR release image and 7238 for the deep
ones, 2.39 and 2.41 ms; five times the deep figure is 12.1 ms, past the
old deadline. The comment also gave the cycles of one image under the
name of another.

20 ms is five times the largest figure with room for some 4700 more
instructions in crust's init, below the 50 ms cap. It costs nothing on a
good boot: the wait ends as soon as crust is up. Only a crust that does
not come up delays the boot, by 20 ms instead of 12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
index 823e13598..b907a7d48 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
@@ -43,11 +43,15 @@ bool sunxi_psci_is_scpi(void)
 #define SUNXI_RTC_GP5			(SUNXI_RTC_BASE + 0x0114)
 
 /*
- * How long crust may take from the reset release to MAGIC and RUNNING: five
- * times the 57432 AR100 cycles crust_emu.py counts for 1957ee6 (SR, 8 cycles
- * per instruction) at 24 MHz, 2.4 ms. The design caps it at 50 ms.
+ * How long crust may take from the reset release to MAGIC and RUNNING. An
+ * instruction-level model of the AR100 (8 cycles per instruction at 24 MHz,
+ * the slowest clock the SPL may leave it on) counts at most 7238
+ * instructions, 2.41 ms, for the crust images of 07.10.2026 (the deep ones;
+ * 2.39 ms for the SR release image). Five times that is 12.1 ms; 20 ms
+ * leaves room for some 4700 more instructions before RUNNING. A crust that
+ * is up ends the wait at once; the cap is 50 ms.
  */
-#define SCP_START_US			12000U
+#define SCP_START_US			20000U
 
 static uint32_t scp_read(unsigned int off)
 {
